            <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.6.2</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<h3>Added</h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Comments column (설명):</b> right-click a Details column header and turn on <b>Comments</b> to see the comments you wrote in Finder's Get Info. The cell shows the comment on one line, and hovering shows all of it. Click the header to sort by comment; items without one come last. Comments fill in after the files appear, so even a big folder on a NAS opens as fast as before, and Refresh reads them again. Free.</li>
<li>Get Info (⌘I) and the Properties window show the item's Finder comment too.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
